  "summary": "Seventeen ML-based expression and spatial omics items, seven published and ten preprints, rose 2.86-fold with no code or industry signal yet recorded.",
  "synthesis": "The activity comprises 17 items, seven published and ten preprints, with a rise ratio of 2.86 and no recorded code, industry, or 7-day star signal. Methods concentrate on spatial transcriptomics: ISPat-3D, DeSPA, SORT, STAVelo, and STARIT apply spatial or image-based models to infer cell-level or gene-program structure. Representation learning appears in ARO (aligned multi-omics for cancer classification), scGEN (adaptive feature weighting for scRNA-seq clustering), and VIMA (variational autoencoder fingerprinting of tissue patches for case-control analysis). Glioma single-cell dynamics recur across scCTM and the H3K27M physics-informed neural network study. The signals describe observed volume only and do not establish drivers of the increase.",
